graham windram was fighting against the  floodwaters to save  his home his 25-ton barge washed onto  the riverbank  in great barford search and rescue  helping him to get it back into the  river  and try to secure it there with all his  belongings  on board it has been a christmas like no  other  i've been quite happily moored there i  live there obviously so  i go to work every day so getting on and  off the boat's been fine  the last two days i had to uh basically  abandon ship  and uh we've had to make precautions now  today  to uh steady the boat for when the  levels drop  you can't see anymore where you would  usually have the banks of the river and  then the fields and  people's gardens and actually if you  drive round this area  it is a similar picture just this  enormous  sea of water and that is why people over  the last couple of days have been urged  to leave their homes of course here they  are still living in tier four  but the police and other agencies say  people need to take whatever precautions  they have to  and not risk their lives from christmas  eve the waters have been rising along  this stretch of the river gretu's  with 1300 people urged to leave their  homes  one of three severe flood warnings in  place with another two  in northamptonshire it was the center of  bedford that was causing concern first  thing  many say it's not been this bad for over  20 years  on christmas night locals dug these  trenches to keep the waters back  jan schofield lives over the road and  says it was like the community spirit of  lockdown  kicked in once again everyone rallied  around last night from about  six o'clock all the way through to three  o'clock this morning  people local neighbours were digging the  trenches  bringing sandbags some guys with big  trucks came and pulled out the huge  trees that you can see over the road  which were getting stuck underneath the  little white bridge the newnan bridge  and that really cleared the waters  people were staying awake all night  obviously not knowing whether it would  come over the road  for those in charge of the response  covid has had to be at the front of  their minds  and they say it still should be for the  rest of us  please don't be heroic please  follow uh the guidelines do not do  anything that's not  a prayer and also hoving's not gone away  this hasn't just suddenly  allowed kobe to disappear bedford's  figures remain  absolutely high overnight large parts of  the country are expected to be hit by  high winds and heavy rain as storm bella  moves in  the potential impact unclear as many  still deal with the impact  of this christmas disruption rihanna  mills  sky news
 

